---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { readSiteEnv } from '../lib/env.mjs';
const { formAction, contactEmail } = readSiteEnv(import.meta.env);
const formHost = formAction ? new URL(formAction).host : null;
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects: aggregate analytics, correction requests you send us, and nothing else. No accounts, no ads, no sale of data." pageType="privacy" crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-11-14.</p>
  <h2>What this site collects</h2>
  <p>This site has no accounts, no ads and no sale of data. Browsing it requires no personal information. The only way personal information reaches us is if you send a correction or removal request (see below).</p>
  <h2>Google Analytics (GA4)</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to measure aggregate traffic. It sets cookies and sends usage data to Google: pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser type, and the page that referred you. Google acts as our processor for this data. We do not enable Google signals or ad personalization, we use the shortest data retention setting offered, we do not set user IDs, and we do not put personal data in events or URLs. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a> for how Google handles this data.</p>
  <p>When Analytics is on, the site also sends four counted events, nothing else: a link to a company's own source page was clicked, the compare button was used, the example rent was changed, and the site search was used. An event carries no search terms, no rent value, no company name and no address; it only counts that the action happened.</p>
  <h2>Google Search Console</h2>
  <p>We use Google Search Console to see aggregate search performance (queries, impressions, clicks). It gives us no data about individual visitors.</p>
  <h2>Search on this site</h2>
  <p>Site search (Pagefind) runs in your browser. Your search terms are not sent to us or to anyone else.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on Vercel, which keeps standard server logs (such as IP address and requested page) for operating and securing the service.</p>
  <h2 id="requests">Correction and removal requests</h2>
  <p>If you ask us to correct, add or remove a listing, we receive the name, role and email address you give us and the evidence link you provide. We use them only to check the request and reply to you. We do not publish them or sell them.{formHost ? <> The form on the <a href="/corrections/">correction page</a> sends what you type to a hosted form service at {formHost}, which stores it for us.</> : null}{contactEmail ? <> If you email {contactEmail} instead, your email provider and ours handle the message.</> : null} We delete a request's contact details 12 months after the request is closed. The public data records only that a removal happened, without requester details.</p>
  <h2>Business information in the directory</h2>
  <p>The directory lists only business information that businesses have published publicly, such as company name, website, business address, phone number and fees, with the source and dates shown for each fact. To correct or remove a listing, use the <a href="/corrections/">correction page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{contactEmail ? <>Email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>, or use the <a href="/corrections/">correction page</a>.</> : <>Use the <a href="/corrections/">correction page</a>.</>}</p>
</Base>
